  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1411.03 Operator Authority",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1411.03 Operator Authority.\n\n(a) The physical operator of a challenge course or zip line shall cease operation of the challenge course or zip line, in a manner that does not endanger the safety of any person operating, riding on, or using the challenge course or zip line, in the event that any such person is acting in a manner that might cause or contribute to the injury of the person or others. The operator shall not recommence operation of the challenge course or zip line until the circumstances justifying the cessation of operations is resolved.\n\n(b) The circumstances justifying the cessation of operations described in (a) above shall include, but not be limited to, all of the following conditions that interfere with public safety:\n\n(1) Drunkenness;\n\n(2) Drug abuse;\n\n(3) Refusal to obey rules posted by the operator for the safe use of the challenge course or zip line;\n\n(4) Engaging in any challenge course or zip line without the authority, supervision, and guidance of the operator and their employees;\n\n(5) Dropping, throwing, or expelling any object from the challenge course or zip line, unless authorized to do so by the operator or their employees;\n\n(6) Performing any act that interferes with the safe operation of a challenge course or zip line; or\n\n(7) Engaging in any harmful conduct or willfully or negligently engaging in any conduct that might cause or contribute to the injury of any person or damage to the challenge course or zip line.\n\nSource. #12615, eff 8-28-18; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1400.html"
